{
  "dom_id": "step-q92783",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133433/assets/1f62f15382a5f5d91ea1e2f56acc973d009316f62bdfd70f61fe131a28e42da1.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of rhombuses to the total number of shapes?",
  "worked_solution": "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $4$ rhombuses.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $8$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to total shapes is $4:8.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,8 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rhombuses to the total shapes is $1:2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
